    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimen Pair\nRaw Amethyst & Banded Agate Geode\nCombined Weight: 1.4 lbs\nThis mineral pairing features a raw purple amethyst crystal cluster alongside a polished banded agate geode specimen. The amethyst exhibits natural crystalline terminations with lavender to violet hues on a characteristic matrix base. The cut agate nodule showcases concentric banding in tones of gray, cream, and brown surrounding a sparkling interior cavity lined with microcrystalline quartz druzy.\nGenuine geological specimens ideal for display, study, or rock collections\nRaw amethyst cluster features multiple light-catching faceted crystal points\nAgate specimen displays a polished cut face highlighting distinct growth rings\nHollow geode center features sparkling druzy quartz with minute mineral inclusions\nLot dimensions approximately 6 x 3.5 x 3 inches\nCondition:\nNatural specimen condition. Both pieces exhibit organic geological textures, uneven matrix edges, and natural mineral fissures. The agate face is polished smooth with an unfinished exterior rind. No artificial repairs or modifications observed.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
